Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Stabilizer Codes in the Quantum Framework", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The framework's stabilizer engine holds a ",
 StyleBox["state", "TI"],
 ": an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 "-qubit state stored as the Pauli operators that fix it, pushed through \
Clifford gates in the Heisenberg picture. This layer holds a ",
 StyleBox["code", "TI"],
 ": a subspace fixed by a commuting group of Pauli checks, chosen so that the \
errors we care about push a state out of that subspace in a way we can detect \
and undo."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference matters. A stabilizer state is fixed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " independent checks and is a single point. A stabilizer code is fixed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "<", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " of them, so it is a subspace of dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 ", and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " qubits' worth of room inside it is where the protected information lives. \
Everything below follows from that one shift."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
What this note covers, in order: the code object and how it is stored; the \
Pauli layer beneath it; the structural quantities (logical operators, \
distance); syndromes and decoding; encoding circuits; building codes out of \
other codes; noise; and the figure of merit the whole subject is about \
\[LongDash] whether a logical qubit survives. Then the same question asked \
honestly: the circuit that measures the checks, the faults inside it, \
detectors, and a memory experiment run over several rounds \[LongDash] ending \
with the whole thing written out in Stim's syntax and checked against it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One thing here is not available anywhere else, and it is worth naming up \
front. Because the noise rate may be left symbolic, the logical error rate \
comes back as an ",
 StyleBox["exact polynomial",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " rather than a sampled estimate. A fast simulator answers \"about 0.0022 at \
p = 0.01\"; this answers \"",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"10", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "2"], "-", "200", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "3"], "/", "9", "+", "160", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "4"], "/", "9", "-", "128", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "5"], "/", "27"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ", for every p\". That is what exactness and symbolic generality buy, and it \
is the one move a Monte Carlo simulator structurally cannot make. It holds \
all the way up: even with every gate, reset and readout of the \
syndrome-extraction circuit failing, the answer is still a closed-form \
polynomial, and the last sections use that to say two things about fault \
tolerance that are awkward to state any other way."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["Definition", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The code layer is a development package under ",
 Cell["OngoingProjects/QEC/", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ", not yet part of the paclet, so this page loads both the framework and the \
layer itself. Symbols introduced in this section stay bound for the whole \
note."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two notes on why this cell exists at all, since documentation pages \
normally have no setup code. A reference page gets an ",
 Cell[BoxData["ExampleInitialization"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " cell from its template, and the converter fills it from the frontmatter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Context", ":"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 "; the tech-note template has no such cell, so the converter has nothing to \
fill and a reader opening the notebook cold would find no context loaded. And \
the code layer is not in any paclet yet, so no context declaration could load \
it. Both lines go away when the layer moves into the paclet."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell["\<\
Load the framework and locate the code layer. The cell reports whether it \
worked, because a setup cell that fails quietly leaves every later cell \
showing an unevaluated symbol \[LongDash] which looks like a broken package \
rather than a path that did not resolve:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qecCore", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"SelectFirst", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\n", "        ", 
       RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
        RowBox[{"beside", " ", "this", " ", 
         RowBox[{"notebook", ":", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"docs", "/", "Tutorials"}], "/", " ", "up"}], " ", "two", 
           " ", "levels"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", "        ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Quiet", " ", "@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Check", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ParentDirectory", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
               "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<QECCore\>\"", ",", 
              " ", "\"\<QECCore.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           "$Failed"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
        RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
          "from", " ", "a", " ", "repo", " ", "checkout", " ", "of", " ", 
           "the", " ", "framework"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
          "when", " ", "that", " ", "is", " ", "the", " ", "one", " ", 
           "loaded"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", "        ", 
        RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ParentDirectory", "[", 
            RowBox[{"DirectoryName", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
              "FindFile", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], ",",
               " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
           "            ", "\"\<OngoingProjects\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QEC\>\"",
            ",", " ", "\"\<QECCore\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<QECCore.wl\>\""}], 
          "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
        RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
         RowBox[{"from", " ", "the", " ", "working", " ", "directory"}], " ", 
         "*)"}], "\n", "        ", 
        RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Directory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<QECCore\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<QECCore.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "    ", "}"}], ",",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"StringQ", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FileExistsQ", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
      "    ", "$Failed"}], "\n", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"If", "[", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qecCore", " ", "===", " ", "$Failed"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<QECCoreNotFound\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<MessageTemplate\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", 
       "        ", "\"\<Could not locate QECCore/QECCore.wl. Get it by hand, \
then run the rest of the page.\>\""}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Get", "[", "qecCore", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"MemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "$ContextPath", ",", " ", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QEC`\>\""}], 
     "]"}]}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]= ",ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " there means the layer is loaded and its symbols are on the context path, \
so every cell below runs. A ",
 Cell[BoxData["Failure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " means only that the file was not where this page guessed: ",
 Cell[BoxData["Get"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " the ",
 Cell["QECCore/QECCore.wl", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " beside it by hand and continue from the next cell."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["The code object", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell["\<\
A code is built from its stabilizer generators, given as Pauli strings. The \
constructor checks what a code needs: equal length, pairwise commuting, \
independent.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell["The five-qubit code, from its four checks:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

