Cell["\<\
Nineteen faults, nineteen distinct signatures, none ambiguous \[LongDash] \
against 288 faults collapsing onto 71 signatures of which 29 carry \
conflicting logical effects. The code did not get worse; the circuit \
measuring it is not fault tolerant.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell["\<\
This is the gap that verified ancillas exist to close, and the book spends a \
chapter on it: cat states (\[Section]12.1.2\[Dash]12.1.3) feeding Shor error \
correction (\[Section]12.2), Steane error correction (\[Section]12.3), Knill \
error correction (\[Section]12.4), with \[Section]12.5 comparing their costs. \
One detail there is a useful target: \[Section]12.3.3 argues Steane error \
correction needs no repeated syndrome measurement at all, because its ancilla \
and measurement errors enter additively. None of these is implemented yet \
\[LongDash] they are roadmap work \[LongDash] and the number above is what it \
costs not to have them.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell["Handing it to Stim", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Stim (",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:2103.02202",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.02202"], None}],
 ") is the community's reference stabilizer simulator, and the source of the \
detector error model as an explicit object. The point of connecting to it \
rather than competing with it is that the two are good at different things: \
it samples fast and large, this layer derives exactly and symbolically. \
Writing the memory experiment out in its syntax buys an independent check on \
all of the above, and a path to the decoders built on top of it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The emitted circuit encodes first \[LongDash] Stim starts in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "0"}], "\[Ellipsis]", "0", "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 ", which is not a codeword for a general code, and a memory experiment that \
does not start inside the code space has a meaningless first round of \
detectors \[LongDash] then runs the noisy rounds, then a noiseless one:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Take", "[", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"StringSplit", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QECStimCircuit", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<BitFlipCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "200"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\n\>\""}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", "14"}], "\n", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"# 3 data qubits, 2 check ancillas, 2 noisy rounds, Z-basis memory\"\
\>"},
    {"\<\"# emitted by QECStimCircuit\"\>"},
    {"\<\"# --- encode ---\"\>"},
    {"\<\"H 1\"\>"},
    {"\<\"H 0\"\>"},
    {"\<\"CZ 1 2\"\>"},
    {"\<\"H 1\"\>"},
    {"\<\"CZ 0 1\"\>"},
    {"\<\"H 0\"\>"},
    {"\<\"# --- round 1 ---\"\>"},
    {"\<\"R 3\"\>"},
    {"\<\"X_ERROR(0.005) 3\"\>"},
    {"\<\"CX 0 3\"\>"},
    {"\<\"DEPOLARIZE2(0.005) 0 3\"\>"}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[60]= ",ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The structure scales as it should: one detector per check per round, plus the \
final noiseless round, and a single logical observable. Three noisy rounds of \
the Steane code's six checks give four layers of six:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"source", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QECStimCircuit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QECCode", "[", "\"\<SteaneCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"QECNoiseModel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Circuit\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "500"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
   ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"StringCount", "[", 
      RowBox[{"source", ",", " ", "\"\<DETECTOR\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"StringCount", "[", 
      RowBox[{"source", ",", " ", "\"\<OBSERVABLE_INCLUDE\>\""}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "\n", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[61]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"24", ",", "1"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[61]= ",ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One asymmetry is deliberate. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECLogicalErrorRate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],
 " asks whether the decoder got the residual error's whole class right, \
covering logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 " and logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 " damage at once, because that is the right question for an unknown logical \
state. A Stim memory experiment is single-basis by construction \[LongDash] \
prepare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "0"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],
 ", keep it, measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 " \[LongDash] so the emitted circuit declares one observable and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Observable\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 " chooses which. The detector part is basis-independent, and that is where \
the two models are compared."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That comparison has been run. Five cases \[LongDash] three at circuit \
level, two at phenomenological, including the non-CSS five-qubit code whose \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 " generators are the only thing exercising the square-root-of-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 " rotation \[LongDash] with 58 detector firing rates and 5 observable flip \
rates computed exactly here and sampled over two million shots there. \
Everything agrees within 2.7 standard errors, and PyMatching decodes every \
exported circuit unchanged, which is a second and structural check: a \
malformed circuit does not produce a detector error model that decomposes \
into a matching graph."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],

Cell["Where this comes from", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every claim above is either computed by the package and checked against an \
independent oracle, or taken from one of these. Section numbers are \
Gottesman's 2026 ",
 StyleBox["Stabilizer Codes and Quantum Error Correction", "TI"],
 " unless the thesis is named."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

